<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Strategic Topography of Czech Brands</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<style>{{ inline_css }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<header class="masthead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Brand Reflection Series &middot; Episode 2 &middot; companion to
        <a href="https://sandovabarbora.github.io/color-fingerprint-cz/" style="color:inherit;">Color fingerprint</a>
        &amp;
        <a href="https://sandovabarbora.github.io/sound-fingerprint-cz/" style="color:inherit;">Sound fingerprint</a>
    </p>
    <h1>Where Czech brands stand, and what's moving around them.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Homepage messaging from {{ counts.n_brands_used }} major Czech brands embedded into a multilingual semantic space alongside {{ counts.n_trends }} top rising Czech queries, projected to 2D. Dense clusters are red oceans. Isolated points are voices. Trends near empty zones are openings.</p>
    <p class="byline">By {{ author }}. <a href="{{ repo_url }}">Source on GitHub</a>.</p>
</header>

<section class="method">
    <p class="method-label">Method</p>
    <p class="method-body">Brand homepage text (title, meta, headings, first paragraphs) extracted via trafilatura. Top rising Czech queries via pytrends with a hand-curated fallback when the unofficial API rate-limits. Both corpora embedded with <code>intfloat/multilingual-e5-base</code> (passage / query prefixes per model docs, L2-normalised). Layout via UMAP (n_neighbors=10, min_dist=0.3, cosine metric). Cluster labels are sector-rolled. Opportunity score = velocity &times; (1 &minus; mean cosine-similarity to the 3 nearest brands), computed in the 768-dim embedding space, not on the 2D map.</p>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">01</span><h2>The map</h2></div>
    <p class="section-intro">Brands are filled circles coloured by cluster. Rising queries are outlined diamonds sized by velocity. Distance on this map is an approximation of semantic distance in 768 dimensions; treat it as topology, not as a metric.</p>
    <figure class="map-frame">
        {{ map_svg | safe }}
        <figcaption class="scatter-cap">UMAP layout. Cluster names appear at each cluster's centroid.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="legend-strip">
{% for chip in legend %}
        <div class="legend-chip">
            <span class="legend-dot" style="background: {{ chip.color }};"></span>
            <div class="legend-meta">
                <p class="legend-name">{{ chip.name }}</p>
                <p class="legend-brands">{{ chip.n_brands }} brands &mdash; {{ chip.brand_examples }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
{% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">02</span><h2>Opportunity table</h2></div>
    <p class="section-intro">The top {{ opportunities | length }} rising queries sorted by <em>velocity &times; (1 &minus; saturation)</em>. High momentum and low brand coverage points to strategic white space. Rows flagged <span class="low-conf-inline">low&#8209;signal</span> are queries whose top three brand matches sit within 0.025 of each other — the "winner" is essentially arbitrary and indicates the trend has no sector match in this corpus (typically travel, streaming, niche topics). Treat those rows as evidence of a corpus gap, not as a recommended brand activation.</p>
    <table class="opp-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Trend</th>
                <th class="num-col">Velocity</th>
                <th>Nearest brands</th>
                <th class="num-col">Saturation</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
{% for o in opportunities %}
            <tr class="{% if o.low_confidence %}opp-low-conf{% endif %}">
                <td class="opp-trend">
                    {{ o.trend }}
                    {% if o.low_confidence %}<span class="low-conf-badge">low signal</span>{% endif %}
                </td>
                <td class="num-col">{{ "%.0f" | format(o.velocity) }}</td>
                <td class="opp-nearby">
                    {{ o.near_brand_1 }}<span class="opp-sim">({{ "%.2f" | format(o.near_brand_1_sim) }})</span>
                    {% if o.near_brand_2 %} &middot; {{ o.near_brand_2 }}<span class="opp-sim">({{ "%.2f" | format(o.near_brand_2_sim) }})</span>{% endif %}
                    {% if o.near_brand_3 %} &middot; {{ o.near_brand_3 }}<span class="opp-sim">({{ "%.2f" | format(o.near_brand_3_sim) }})</span>{% endif %}
                </td>
                <td class="num-col">{{ "%.2f" | format(o.saturation_score) }}</td>
            </tr>
{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>

{% if insights %}
<section>
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">03</span><h2>Observations</h2></div>
    <div class="patterns">
{% for ins in insights %}
        <article class="pattern">
            <p class="num">{{ "%02d" | format(loop.index) }}</p>
            <div>
                <h3>{{ ins.title }}</h3>
                <p class="evidence">{{ ins.body }}</p>
            </div>
        </article>
{% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<footer>
    <div>
        <h4>Brand Reflection Series</h4>
        <p>Episode 1 &mdash; <a href="https://sandovabarbora.github.io/color-fingerprint-cz/">Color fingerprint</a> (visual analysis of TV spots)</p>
        <p>Episode 1.5 &mdash; <a href="https://sandovabarbora.github.io/sound-fingerprint-cz/">Sound fingerprint</a> (audio analysis)</p>
        <p>Episode 2 (this) &mdash; Strategic topography (semantic analysis of homepage messaging)</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h4>Code</h4>
        <p><a href="{{ repo_url }}">strategic-topography-cz</a></p>
        <p>MIT for code, CC&#8209;BY&#8209;4.0 for derived data.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h4>Disclaimer</h4>
        <p>Analysis of publicly available brand communication. Brands are referenced for analytical purposes only. Positioning reflects current homepage messaging at time of scrape. No agency attribution is implied.</p>
    </div>
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
